		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">59</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">
Following are some hints to put the logic in words.

1. As I process 1000 values, it will be difficult for me to remember all the elements of array, so I will write down all the numbers in a paper.
2. Then I see I have to fold the array 20 times.
3. It is difficult for me to remember the elements of the array after every folds. So I wrote down the elements after each fold in paper.
4. Here I have observed that while folding the array there is relation between index of elements and length of array. Suppose if first element index value is i then its pair will have index value length of array minus i minus 1.

Following is what I came up with.</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">1406.4170620916184</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">5864.825518147089</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">348.4091545813991</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">254.482998015921</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">
Following are some hints to put the logic in words.

1. As I process 1000 values, it will be difficult for me to remember all the elements of array, so I will write down all the numbers in a paper.
2. Then I see I have to fold the array 20 times.
3. It is difficult for me to remember the elements of the array after every folds. So I wrote down the elements after each fold in paper.
4. Here I have observed that while folding the array there is relation between index of elements and length of array. Suppose if first element index value is i then its pair will have index value length of array minus i minus 1.

Following is what I came up with.</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontSize" type="int">12</attribute>
				<attribute key="fontName" type="String">Dialog</attribute>
				<attribute key="configuration" type="String">CroppingLabel</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentWidth" type="double">348.4091545813991</attribute>
				<attribute key="contentHeight" type="double">247.5</attribute>
				<attribute key="autoSizePolicy" type="String">node_width</attribute>
				<attribute key="anchor" type="String">c</attribute>
			</section>
		</section>
		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">60</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following is what I come up with

1. Read the size of array from input
2. Create an empty array
3. Read the next value from input
4. Append it to the array
5. Repeat steps 3 and 4 until you read all values 
6. Read the last line of input i.e. number of folds.
Phase 2
7. Create a variable called len and store length of array in it.
8. Create an empty array called resArr.
9. Create a variable i and initialize it to 0
10. Now add element at index i and element at index at len-i-1 (why not len - i?)
11. Now increment the value i.
12. Repeat step 9 and 10 untill 'i' reach middle element of array.
13. Now check if len is odd or even.
13.1 If len is odd then, then append middle element of array to resArr, otherwise do nothing.
14. Repeat step 8,9,10,11,12,13 untill the array is fold numOfFolds time.
15. Now display the length of the final array.
16. Now display all the elements of final array line by line.</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">1205.225863420265</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">6202.270897303568</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">779.4444030331657</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">303.00541654703636</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Following is what I come up with

1. Read the size of array from input
2. Create an empty array
3. Read the next value from input
4. Append it to the array
5. Repeat steps 3 and 4 until you read all values 
6. Read the last line of input i.e. number of folds.
Phase 2
7. Create a variable called len and store length of array in it.
8. Create an empty array called resArr.
9. Create a variable i and initialize it to 0
10. Now add element at index i and element at index at len-i-1 (why not len - i?)
11. Now increment the value i.
12. Repeat step 9 and 10 untill 'i' reach middle element of array.
13. Now check if len is odd or even.
13.1 If len is odd then, then append middle element of array to resArr, otherwise do nothing.
14. Repeat step 8,9,10,11,12,13 untill the array is fold numOfFolds time.
15. Now display the length of the final array.
16. Now display all the elements of final array line by line.</attribute>
